   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 1. Capture a RefCap\nA **RefCap** (reference capture) records what MiniMax H3 takes from reference photos into one file in `ComfyUI/models/refcaps/`: the photos' VAE latents and the photos the text encoder saw, plus its `<Picture i>` rows with `store_rows` (only *H3 RefCap Apply* needs them). Nothing is changed, so replaying it (workflow 2) matches the reference node fed the original photos, with no photo loaders, resizing or VAE encode.\n\n**Steps**\n1. Load **up to 9 photos** of one person (5 are wired here). To add one, connect it to the next `ref_image` slot **and** the next `image_N` input.\n2. Connect the **same photos in the same order** to both nodes. The reference node makes the rows and latents; H3 RefCap Capture also stores the resized photos, which *H3 RefCap Replay* needs.\n3. Leave the reference node's **prompt empty**. Capture rejects conditioning that ends in prompt text.\n4. Set **width / height** to the size you will generate at. With `ref_image_size` = `match`, each photo is scaled to that pixel area, and the RefCap keeps that size. For the most identity, use `max` with photos of about 1024 px: +0.06 face similarity in tests, but ~2.2x the render time and ~33 MB per photo.\n5. Set `name` and queue. *Capture summary* shows the photo count, rows, reference tokens and file size.\n\n**Choosing photos**\n- One person, face clearly visible, varied angles and expressions: front, 3/4 left and right, neutral and smiling.\n- Same age and look across the photos. Avoid sunglasses, heavy filters, group shots and tiny faces.\n- In the tests, white t-shirts in the photos did not leak into renders that asked for other clothes.\n- Only use people who agreed to it.\n\n**File contents** (safetensors, format `h3_refcap`): `ref_0..` latents, the photos (as PNGs with `compact`, which replay bit-identically; a 1024 px photo is about 0.7 MB instead of 12 MB), `rows` and `tags` with `store_rows` (about 20 MB per 1,000 rows), JSON metadata."
   ],
